          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What are called
            %em matrix product states
            (MPS) in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            (specifically in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            and in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network+states"} tensor network states
            of the form of a ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensors"} tensors
            all of rank 3.
          %p
            For example, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            (with
            = succeed "-notation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "metric+Lie+algebra#Definition"} there
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor"} tensor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \coloneqq [-,-] \in \mathfrak{g}^\ast \otimes \mathfrak{g}^\ast \otimes \mathfrak{g}
            gives rise to matrix product states of the following form:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MatrixProductStateFromMetricLieAlgebra.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
